<title>FINLAND: POSTIPANKKI TO CUT PRIME RATE TO 4.25 PCT.</title>
<headline>POSTIPANKKI TO CUT PRIME RATE TO 4.25 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish state-owned bank Postipankki Oy said in a statement on Wednesday it will lower its prime interest rate to 4.25 percent from 4.50 percent on December 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The reason for the change in the prime rate is a decline in market interest rates,&quot; Postipankki said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
